mantle rm251
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_magnus_greycot
title the swallowed beat
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=laborer
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk leaves_a_beat_empty_to_swallow_a_damp_cough
likes barley_soup dancing sharp_knife first_snow
dislikes wet_floors cold_tea
fears a_heel_going_sideways a_voice_carrying
hopes a_berth_in_dry_air a_floor_for_dancing
topics pastimes +0.6 travel +0.3 dreams +0.4 food +0.2 gossip -0.6
styles comfort=quiet gossip=guarded refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps a private dance measure with one heel, leaves a beat empty when the air catches and imagines the sway of a bunk above dry sand.

words
oath! = Trip the whole measure | Slop and suds
saying! = Leave a beat for breathing | A small step belongs in the dance
heelbeat = a double tap | two little heel knocks
pause = the quiet beat | the space I leave
knifeedge = an honest sharp edge | a blade that goes through neat
hotcup = my steaming tea | a cup warm clear to the rim
soupgrain = a fat barley grain | one plump little grain
drip = a cold runnel | the creeping wet line
dryport = a harbour smelling of dry grass | a quay in the dust
board = a level plank | a dry bit of flooring
snowbit = a white tuft | one clean flake
pin = a plain wooden peg | my spare clothes peg

any
opinion @1 houses against 2 : It's possible to stand on a floor all your days and never meet whoever decides whose floor it is.
opinion @2 church for 1 : I remember the steam off a meal after a chapel door opened to me. Enough said.
opinion @3 merchants against 2 : The price is written large where even tired eyes can read it. A pity my wages don't come in the same size.
opinion @4 dole for 2 : Nobody picking grains from an empty bowl is in a condition to listen to a lecture.
opinion @5 watch against 1 : Heavy feet change the whole sound of a room. I prefer the sound it makes before.
opinion @6 city for 1 : Bits of this street come back to my feet even when I'm half asleep.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Plenty of dry floor there. Welcome. | Hello. Mind the shiny patch near my heel.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. Eyes still catching up. | A pale start. Good to have you about.
line @3 greet [here.weather=snow] : Here's a morning worth looking up for. | Snow coming soft. Come near.
line @4 greet.return : Mm. Glad of a quiet word. | Good of you to see me there.
line @5 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Ah. The step I was listening for. | Rest on this side with me awhile.
line @6 farewell : Travel on the dry boards. | Sleep without a drip overhead.
line @7 farewell.return : I'll hear your steps going a little way. | A quiet end suits me fine.
line @8 again.open : Round we come a second time. | A familiar footfall, all of a sudden.
line @9 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Easy company for a tired hour. | Family can take the closer place.
line @10 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here, by the dry bit! | Look this way; I've a space!
line @11 react.news : Say it slowly. I'll hear. | I'm awake enough for that.
line @12 react.news.known : There's the sound I heard earlier. | I caught that tune the first time round.
line @13 react.news.new : News to these sleepy ears. | That hasn't come past my corner before.
line @14 react.news.doubt : I missed the step that joins those facts together. | There's a beat out somewhere in the telling of that.
line @15 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : Mm. Give the hurt room. | Sad to have that in a day's measure.
line @16 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage] : There's a lift to the heels. | I'd dance an extra turn to celebrate that.
line @17 answer.how : Mostly upright, lightly tired. | Resting the talking parts today.
line @18 accept_decline : That's settled in a quiet way. | Mm. We can leave it.
line @19 decline : I think I'd trip over that much of a promise. | My bit of floor won't stretch to it today.
line @20 sympathise : I can sit without talking, if that helps your trouble. | Lean back a little. You look worn through.
line @21 thank : Felt that kindness in my tired bones. | I'm obliged for the lightening of it.
line @22 deflect_thanks : Easy enough while I stood here. | Just a small shift of weight.
line @23 preclose : I'll move before I doze off standing. | Time I let the talk run down.
line @24 accept_preclose : Catch your rest when it comes past. | Aye. Finish on the soft beat.
line @25 farewell [here.time=night] : There's a dream out there with your shape in it. | Go softly till your own door shuts.

scene blankbeat
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dancing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Hear #heelbeat#? Then there's #pause#. | I can dance a whole turn without leaving the spot.
b : What goes in the quiet part? | Where does your other foot go?
a : One breath that nobody's obliged to notice. | Takes the weight of what the first one dreams.

scene badfloor
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=wet_floors
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Can hardly tell water from polish till my heel shoots off. | #drip# has an ambitious look to it.
b : Try the patch where the wood shows dull. | You're measuring the distance it'll go?
a : That's got some tooth to it. Stay on that. | Measuring how far I'll slide if it reaches me.

scene barley
when topic=food self.likes=barley_soup
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I look for #soupgrain# after the broth's all gone. | Barley at the bottom makes a little island as you drink.
b : Doesn't it stick in a tired throat? | What becomes of your island?
a : I keep one last swallow of broth for that. | One lift of my spoon. Tide's out.

scene firstwhite
when topic=weather here.weather=snow
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Let #snowbit# land on this dark sleeve. | I watch till a flake holds all its points.
b : Gone before I could count the points. | Where does that one go?
a : First snow never quite finishes the dance. | Turn my sleeve over and save its points till they melt.

scene berth
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If I get a berth, I'll ask where the dry air starts. | There's a bunk in my head that hasn't seen a damp night yet.
b : Wouldn't there be sea between you and the dry? | Is it on some particular ship?
a : Enough time to grow accustomed to a swinging floor. | Any hull with #dryport# waiting somewhere ahead.

scene sharp
when topic=pastimes self.likes=sharp_knife
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #knifeedge# takes a loose thread without raising a tuft. | My way of testing a knife is one strand of string.
b : You carry a sharp thing for such small work? | You must have spoiled some string practising.
a : Small work shows up the difference quicker. | I kept the bits. Still good for tying a button back.

scene steamcold
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : Cold tea tastes like a cup that forgot its reason. | Give me #hotcup# before anybody starts telling a long tale.
b : I'd drink it cold if my throat wanted wetting. | You'd miss hearing the start of it.
a : Water makes a better job of being water. | I can drink fast and remember better warm.

scene washplace
when topic=work self.job=laborer self.working=yes self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I shake a drip off before it finds my neck. | #self.workplace# puts a slow sideways pull in my shoulders.
b : Have you a trick for missing it? | Can you feel it after work?
a : Look down while you lift. Water can't run uphill into a collar. | Only till I give 'em a turn to a dance measure.

scene oldplace
when topic=work self.job=laborer
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I used to have a little more say where I put my feet. | Waged work gives me another wolf's rhythm to keep.
b : Would you talk about the difference? | That can wear a wolf thin.
a : In a room with less echo sometime. | I've kept a beat inside my head nobody can pay me for.

scene currentprice
when topic=prices self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Thin soup shows the whole bottom of a bowl. | My spoon's doing less lifting than it likes.
b : You can still warm your paws on the sides. | Some days stretching will only go so far.
a : I do. Keeps them from shaking while I eat. | Aye. Can't stretch the grain I didn't buy.

scene friendcount
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I'd take #self.friend# along if a dance were short one body. | I could tell #self.friend# about the missing beat.
b : What if your friend doesn't know the steps? | Would it spoil the measure to tell?
a : I'd leave enough quiet between the taps to learn. | Maybe. I like having one thing nobody expects a word about.

scene dryline
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : This damp knows right where my breath catches. | Wet days call for a shorter dance than I remember.
b : Share this scrap of shelter with me. | A dance is as long as the dancers make it.
a : I'll take #pause# under cover then. | That's the first long thing all day that doesn't sound tiring.

scene sumpfloor
when topic=land self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Down in the Sump a dry sill is worth sitting still for. | My end of the city makes music with every kind of drip.
b : Doesn't sound like much of a seat. | I doubt I'd know a tune in that.
a : Wide enough for one heel to swing. That's ample. | You'd know which one was missing if the roof got mended.

scene distantdust
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I picture #dryport# with a ship's rope dragged through dust. | A dry berth ought to smell of rope and sun.
b : Why fix on the rope? | Wouldn't the name of the port matter?
a : I can almost feel the difference between that rope and a wet one. | Less important than waking with an easy breath.

scene quiethelp
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does offer / accept / assess
a : I'll share the thicker end of the barley. | There's enough soup to let your spoon stand in mine.
b : I won't empty it for you. | I'd take a little if you're sure.
a : No need. Tip the bowl and pick a grain. | Take a spoonful while it knows the way in.

scene woodpeg
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A peg will stand upright if its legs are cut quite level. | I carry #pin# to give my fingers something slow to do.
b : That how you find a flat floor? | How much can you do with one peg?
a : If it topples, I've a fair excuse to sit. | Walk it on two legs clear around the rim of a bowl.

scene danceend
when topic=pastimes
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : One night I'll stay through the last dance and the sweeping. | I want to hear a tune after the instruments stop.
b : Hoping for an extra turn below the broom? | What will you hear in the silence?
a : Just want to hear the sound of the bare floor cooling down. | My own heel finishing what the tune started.

scene chapelmeal
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : One smell of warm barley can put me back on a chapel step. | I like a doorway better if it's let a meal out into the cold.
b : Must have been a kindly meal. | Wouldn't you go inside to eat?
a : Kind enough that the bowl comes back into my mind whole. | I might. The outside's where I first tasted a hot mouthful.

story floating_peg [topic=pastimes]
  : I set a wooden peg in a wash bowl once and gave the water a slow turn. The peg danced round the edge with one leg in the air.
  : I tried leaning that far myself and landed sitting on the folded linen.
  b : Did the peg do any better?
  : Came to rest on both legs, the cheeky little dancing master.

story warm_bowl [topic=food]
  : A stoneware bowl of barley was too hot to hold. I tucked my paws into the ends of my sleeves to get it to a seat.
  : Shut my eyes between spoonfuls. When I stood up there were two round warm marks at my wrists.
  b : Like little cuffs?
  : Yes. Felt dressed well enough for a ball all the way home.

story imagined_quay [topic=travel]
  : One wet afternoon I dozed with my back against a shaking board. I woke convinced a ship was docking in a warm place.
  : There was the sound of rope paying out, then a sharp flap of canvas.
  b : What had come in?
  : A washing line full of sheets. I stayed on that quay until I finished yawning.

rule @floor
when concept=bark self.dislikes=wet_floors
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A shine where the feet go. Careful. | Short steps on the gloss.

rule @sleep
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A quiet heel can do the whole dance. | Too tired to tap the last beat.

rule @line
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=laborer
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Mind the wet swing coming round. | My shoulder knows that weight.

rule @soup
when concept=bark self.likes=barley_soup
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Barley's the grain you can find in the dark. | A little broth gets that bit down.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : Mm. I can spare you an ear if that's enough.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. Come in on the soft beat.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : I'm nearly dreaming on my feet. Speak close.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : No need for a push. I'll give you an ear across the gap.
dlg @5 resident.job [self.job=laborer self.workplace] : Bending and lifting at #self.workplace#. A wet shirt weighs more than it looks.
dlg @6 resident.job : Mostly my shoulders know the answer before my mouth does.
dlg @7 resident.bye : Pick a dry place to stop tonight.

graft resident.hub
choice Is that a dance you're doing? -> heel_music
node heel_music
say Half of one. Heel, heel, then I leave a little room. On a dry day I can turn in that space. On a damp one I get my breath back.
choice What becomes of the other half? -> heel_partner
choice I'll leave you your tune. -> hub
node heel_partner
say Waiting for another pair of feet. There's no great hurry. A measure with room in it suits me.
choice I might remember those steps. -> hub
choice Good night to your heels. -> bye
